<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle trade not well tested - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle trade not well tested - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading was at a virtual standstill Monday, USDA said. Buyer inquiry moderate, but most not expressing a bid. Seller interest light, many offering to sell at 104.00 and higher.</p>
<p>Confirmed - 200  Last Week - 300  Last Year - 100</p>
<p>Wk To Date- 300  Sm Pd Lst Wk - 5,500 Sm Pd Lst Yr - 1,600</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered (paid on hot carcass weights)</p>
<p>Steers - Select and Choice 2-3 1225-1250 lbs - few 102.00.</p>
<p>Heifers - No reported sales.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
